{
  "version": "schemaxis.readiness/1",
  "routes": {
    "schemaxis.pandoc/1": {
      "guide": "docs/pandoc.md",
      "context": {
        "purpose": "Publish small structured reports as standalone HTML and editable DOCX, including literal timed transcripts with millisecond-exact integer or HH:MM:SS.mmm columns and explicit draft or declared-review provenance. All-cues-deleted reviewed/2 or reviewed/3 sources publish provenance without a cue table.",
        "assumptions": "Plain single-space text, one-row table headers, bounded local RGB/RGBA PNG imagery; default Pandoc typography. A transcript block names one retained whisper.cpp segments.json (closed machine-draft or author-declared reviewed/1, reviewed/2 or reviewed/3 contract; unsupported versions and extra members are refused). An image block source may also be the typed PNG artifact of an earlier workflow step (for example the WebP decodeToPng route); the PNG is captured and held to the same limits as a path. An optional metadata object declares up to 8 distinct plain-text authors and a description.",
        "constraints": "Up to 32 sections,128 content blocks, 65536 characters,8 images; heading levels 1–3 start at 1 and increase by at most 1. No authored markup/scripts/styles/templates/filters. Transcript blocks: at most 2 per report, 4 MiB each, 512 cues in total, 256 characters per cue; larger documents are refused, never truncated. The file is read at run time, never when planning. Each transcript block may set timeFormat milliseconds or timecode; absent keeps the millisecond columns exactly. metadata holds only authors (1-8 names of at most 100 characters, no semicolon, no repeats) and description (at most 1000 characters), counted in the 65536 character report budget; absent metadata changes nothing.",
        "inspection": "Compare ordered headings, paragraph text, complete table cells and image alt/media bytes in HTML, independent OOXML and fresh native DOCX JSON readback. Inspect the report-summary loss policy and generated documents. A transcript block is checked as the provenance paragraph and, when cues remain, the cue table from the retained captured bytes; the captured bytes, their digest and the optional pin are verified again. An explicit timeFormat is bound in the plan, the capture record and the report summary, and the start/end cells and their column headers are recomputed from the retained bytes. Bound transcriptObservations state the actual reviewed/2 deletion and table shape and the reviewed/3 author-declared timing edits; Pandoc checks this mapping for internal consistency without reopening the original machine draft. A handed-over PNG is captured from the producer's verified publication and compared byte for byte with the HTML data URI and the DOCX and EPUB media; its pixel colour and geometry readback are those of any captured PNG. The producer evidence is verified again, so a changed producer artifact is refused. A metadata declaration is bound in the plan, the capture record (text, character count and SHA-256) and the summary, and each format is read back independently: HTML author/description meta elements and title-block author lines, DOCX core-properties creator (joined with \"; \") and description plus Author-style paragraphs and the fresh Word readback authors, EPUB OPF dc:creator/role/dc:description, title-page author lines and the fresh EPUB readback (whose author order Pandoc 3.12.1 reverses). A missing, extra, stale, reordered or forged author or description in any format fails verification even with refreshed hashes.",
        "recovery": "INVALID_REPORT_TABLE needs rectangular rows; INVALID_HEADING_ORDER needs an outline starting at 1. INVALID_REPORT_IMAGE needs an absolute regular plain RGB/RGBA PNG and a widthMm of at most five decimal places; a widthMm above 148 mm is an INVALID_ARGUMENT range fault. INVALID_REPORT_TEXT needs single-space plain text. INTERPRETER_NOT_FOUND needs configured Pandoc; UNSUPPORTED_NATIVE_BUILD needs the official self-contained Pandoc binary (distribution builds without embedded data files cannot run the sandboxed writers); retained logs and failed result explain native faults. TRANSCRIPT_SOURCE_MISSING and TRANSCRIPT_SOURCE_INVALID need an existing regular segments.json (not a link or directory) of at most 4 MiB; INVALID_TRANSCRIPT_SOURCE needs an absolute .json path without parent references; TIMED_TEXT_* faults mean the file does not satisfy the declared machine-draft or reviewed timed-text contract (UNSUPPORTED_VERSION, UNKNOWN_KEY, REVIEW_UNSUPPORTED, TIMING, CUE_TEXT, RESOURCE_LIMIT, INVALID_JSON, DIGEST_MISMATCH) and the location names the member or cue; REPORT_RESOURCE_LIMIT needs fewer transcripts, cues or characters. An unknown or non-text timeFormat is an INVALID_ARGUMENT fault at planning, before any file or native step; use milliseconds or timecode. A TYPE_MISMATCH fault at a report hand-off names an artifact kind the route does not accept (only text, for transcripts, and image); a text artifact at an image source is INVALID_REPORT_IMAGE because its path does not end in .png. A producer PNG above 4 MiB (8 MiB in total) is refused, never rescaled; the WebP route's own 5 MiB output cap therefore does not guarantee that every decoded PNG fits. An INVALID_ARGUMENT at $.metadata (or $.metadata.authors[i], $.metadata.description) needs the documented type, length, no semicolon in an author and no repeated author; an UNKNOWN_ARGUMENT at $.metadata means a key other than authors and description was supplied; a MISSING_ARGUMENT at $.metadata means the object was empty (omit it); INVALID_REPORT_TEXT there needs single-space plain text."
      },
